# Expectation record for 04_bitfields/005_straddling_and_zero_width.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 005_straddling_and_zero_width
area               = 04_bitfields
description        = Fields straddling an allocation-unit boundary, zero-width separators and unnamed padding
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
Byte images are printed only for structs whose every bit is covered by a named field, so no
unspecified padding bit is ever observed; the zero-width and unnamed-field structs, which
necessarily contain padding, are observed only through sizeof, _Alignof and named-member
read-back.  Every stored value is inside its field's range.  Each field has an explicit
signed or unsigned base type.  Every property is computed twice, once from literal constants and once from
volatile-qualified storage, so the constant folder's answer cannot stand in for the
one the backend computes at run time.
No header is included and printf is declared by hand, so nothing here depends on a
standard-library header bcc does not ship.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
Where a field is placed inside its allocation unit is implementation-defined.  Every bit
position this program asserts is the placement measured on all four targets under test
rather than a guarantee the standard makes, which is what makes the byte images
comparable across backends; the program is compared on all four targets rather than
restricted, and the measured agreement is the reason.
END
expected_stdout    <<END
size_cover32=4 align_cover32=4
size_cover64=8 align_cover64=4
size_nostraddle=12 align_nostraddle=4
size_nozero=4 size_onezero=8 size_twozero=12
size_unnamedpad=4 align_unnamedpad=4
size_signedstraddle=4 align_signedstraddle=4
cover32_read a=5 b=21 c=300 d=20000
cover32_image ad 2c 41 9c
cover32_after_c a=5 b=21 c=511 d=20000
cover32_image_after_c ad ff 41 9c
cover32_c_zero a=5 b=21 c=0 d=20000
cover32_image_c_zero ad 00 40 9c
cover64_read a=7 b=31 c=511 d=32767 e=2047 f=2097151
cover64_all_ones ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff
cover64_mixed a=5 b=21 c=300 d=20000 e=1365 f=1398101
cover64_image ad 2c 41 9c 55 ad aa aa
nostraddle_read a=703710 b=74565 c=6785451
nostraddle_after_b a=703710 b=1048575 c=6785451
nozero_read a=21 b=10
onezero_read a=21 b=10
